  "description": "Automatically converts DateTime values to UTC when writing to PostgreSQL and ensures\n      all DateTime values read back are marked as DateTimeKind.Utc.\n      Supports raw Npgsql, Dapper, and EF Core.\n      Optional TimeZoneId converts UTC reads to any IANA timezone (e.g. \"Asia/Manila\", \"America/Los_Angeles\").",
  "id": "ChronoSafe.Npgsql",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-14T20:37:56.287Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "cp6klQYN179j/GD6ur6Vlk4WAOq2gfRsH5UqnFnMzmQf29OVrqS/wmHqP5VTYfkCyqlsNveXv1WHNUSKR1bS1A==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 23808,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Yohann01/ChronoSafe.Npgsql",
  "published": "2026-08-14T20:35:18.393Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0\n      - New: TimeZoneId option on ChronoSafeOptions accepts any IANA timezone ID (e.g. \"Asia/Manila\",\n        \"America/Los_Angeles\") and automatically converts all DateTime values from UTC to the target\n        timezone on read. DST-aware. Validated at startup — throws TimeZoneNotFoundException immediately\n        on an unrecognised ID. Applies to both EF Core and Dapper.\n\n      v1.0.1\n      - Fixed: PostgreSQL connection error \"invalid command-line argument for server process: TimeZone=UTC\".\n        The options startup parameter now correctly uses the -c TimeZone=UTC format required by PostgreSQL.\n        This fix resolves compatibility issues with Neon, Supabase, and direct PostgreSQL connections.",
